      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Philippe Leroux was born in Boulogne Billancourt (France) in 1959.\r\n\r\nIn 1978 he entered the Paris Conservatory (Conservatoire National Supérieur de Musique), studied with Ivo Malec, Claude Ballif, Pierre Schäeffer and Guy Reibel and obtained three first prizes. Meanwhile, he followed classes with Olivier Messiaen, Franco Donatoni, Betsy Jolas, Jean-Claude Eloy and Iannis Xénakis. In 1993 he was selected to enter the Villa Medicis in Rome for two years, where he remained until 1995.\r\n\r\nHis compositional output (about seventy works to date) includes symphonic, vocal, electronic,..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ]
