    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "François Houle is one of today’s most inventive musicians, in all of the diverse musical spheres he embraces: classical, jazz, new music, improvised music, and world music. His extensive touring has led to solo appearances at major festivals across Canada, the United States of America and Europe, and he has released more than a dozen recordings, earning multiple Juno Award and West Coast Music Award nominations. In 2006, François was the featured soloist in Lutoslawski’s Dance Preludes with the CBC Radio Orchestra, a performance hailed by the Los Angeles Times. In 2007, he composed..."
      }
    ],
