    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A classically-trained violist, Jean René spent six years in Italy (opera and symphony orchestras).On his return to Canada, he studied composition at the Université de Montréal and conducting at the Conservatoire de musique de Montréal. Viola soloist with the Orchestre Métropolitain from 1992 to 2002, he has also freelanced with numerous orchestras and chamber music groups. He has also appeared on stage in dance (Bataille, Ani*mâles, Treize lunes and Les Chemins de traverse) and theater (Zulù Time, La nuit des Rois, The Busker's Opera, La cerisaie). At the same time, he has continued..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ]
