    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Alejandro Padilla"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/givenName": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Alejandro"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/familyName": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Padilla"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Alejandro Javier Padilla Gallegos (Monterrey, Nuevo León). Composer and guitarist. For 5 years (2003-2007) he was coordinator of the Composer Center of Nuevo León, the main agency dedicated to the dissemination of contemporary music in the north of the country. He is founder of the International Festival of Contemporary Music \"New Music\" of CONARTE.\r\n\r\nHe was Coordinator of Music and Theater of the Arts of CONARTE from 2008 to July 2012. Winner of the Creators with Trajectory scholarship in 2013. Artistic Coordinator of the Composer Center of Nuevo León, generation 2014-2015. As a..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g12830820",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/artists/eduardo-caballero"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/artists/eduardo-caballero"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Eduardo Caballero"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/givenName": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Eduardo"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/familyName": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Caballero"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Mexican composer and sound artist, His musical studies have been in Mexico, the United States and Spain, his main teachers have been Ramiro L. Guerra, Victor Rasgado, Ignacio Baca Lobera, John Mallia and Mauricio Sotelo. He has taken master classes with composers Beat Furrer, Yan Marez, José Luis Castillo, Carola Bauckhold, and Joao Pedro Oliveira. He has been a member since 2019 of the National System of Creators of FONCA, has received, among others, the following recognitions: UANL Award for Arts 2021 - Auditory Arts, Nuevo León 2021 System for Artistic Impulse and Creation CONARTE,..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g12830840",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.sophiedupuismusic.com/about"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/sameAs": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.sophiedupuismusic.com/about"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://www.instagram.com/sophdupuis/"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC5d5eybCtFmARnUs6DRlrFw?view_as=subscriber"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://www.facebook.com/sophie.dupuis.357"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/artists/sophie-dupuis"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Sophie Dupuis"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/givenName": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Sophie"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/familyName": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Dupuis"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Sophie Dupuis is a francophone composer from and based in New Brunswick, interested in interdisciplinary art music, opera and voice, electroacoustic and acoustic music. She finds her inspiration in the picturesque scenery of the Maritimes where she grew up, in her attraction to raw electrical sounds and to various forms of performance art. Her works have been commissioned and performed by soloists and groups such as Duo Holz, The Art Song Project, Made in Trio, Din of Shadows, Caution Tape Sound Collective, Thin Edge New Music Collective, ECM+ and Esprit Orchestra.Sophie received a Karen Kieser Prize in Canadian Music from the University of Toronto and several prizes for her studies in music, including the University Medal in Music from Dalhousie University, an Ontario Graduate Scholarship, the John Weinzweig Graduate Scholarship and the Theodoros Mirkopoulos Fellowship in Composition two years in a row. She was chosen by composer James Rolfe to receive the 2019 Johanna Metcalf Performing Arts Prize Protégée award. Sophie recently completed her graduate degree and is now working on developing her skills with live and fixed electroacoustics. Aside from her activities as a composer, she works as a violinist, arranger and music educator of violin, piano and theory. She is actively engaged in her community as a volunteer, notably with her role as President of the Canadian League of Composers since 2020.Sophie holds a Bachelor of Music in composition from Dalhousie University, and a Masters of Music and Doctorate of Musical Arts in composition from the University of Toronto."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g12830860",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/artists/genevieve-ackerman"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/artists/genevieve-ackerman"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Geneviève Ackerman"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/givenName": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Geneviève"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/familyName": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Ackerman"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Après avoir terminé un 1er cycle au Conservatoire de musique de Montréal en composition, Geneviève fonde une troupe de théâtre musical, « Le Théâtre du Radeau », un espace de rencontre entre la poésie, le théâtre, la musique et la danse. Profondément marquée par les travaux de Meyerhold, d’Antonin Artaud, de Grotowski, et de Piña Bausch, elle fonde ce théâtre essentiellement expérimental dans l’idée de poursuivre le travail de recherche sur la matière théâtrale qui s’est mis en branle tout au long du XXème siècle, tout en prenant racine dans la tragédie..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ]
  },
