      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Born in 1959 in Prague, Martin Smolka entered the world of music in the early 1980s when he and Miroslav Pudlák (joined later by Petr Kofroň) founded Agon, an ensemble that in the late 80s and early 90s was the most significant mediator of the world's musical avant-garde in the Czech scene, which at the time was dominated by the officially backed domestic pseudo-modernism. From the very outset of his career as a composer, we can discern Smolka's having been influenced by post-Webernism, Minimalism, American experimental music and the Polish School.\r\n\r\nIn the early 90s Smolka was..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ]
  },
