    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Adrianne Munden-Dixon is a violinist, improviser, and composer known for her “shapeshifting technical facility” (I Care If You Listen). Her work often explores the interaction of timbre, texture, and energy with a combination of playfulness and “white-knuckle energy” (Bandcamp Daily). She has given solo performances at Roulette Intermedium, the Dimenna Center, Princeton University and presented her music at the Darmstadt Summer Course and University of Georgia. She is a founding member of Desdemona and has recently worked with the JACK Quartet, Ensemble SuperMusique, Cassie Wieland,..."
      }
