    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Pablo Jiménez is a double bassist and composer born in Bogota and based in Montreal. Using improvisation as a creative engine, his work seeks to establish a rigorous musical language based on movement. He frequently collaborates with ensembles and musicians from the Canadian creative music scene, notably with the Ensemble SuperMusique, Malcolm Goldstein, Lori Freedman and Scott Thomson. He has performed and participated in festivals such as the Festival International de Musique Actuelle de Victoriaville (with Guy Thouin and Ensemble Infini), Suoni per il Popolo, and the Darmstädter Ferienkurse, where he studied with and performed the music of Anthony Braxton."
      }
