    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Wally Gunn is a composer who makes use of patterns and processes in his work, and sometimes utilizes speech, gesture, and movement to heighten the theatricality of musical performance, all with the aim of creating music that is expressive and affecting.&nbsp;The extramusical themes in his work look outward to explore the natural world, and inward to reflect queer identity&nbsp;and experience.&nbsp;Hailing from rural Australia, Wally first played in rock bands, then attended Victorian College of the Arts in Melbourne, before moving to New York to study at Manhattan School of Music, and then..."
      }
    ],
