    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Conductor and pianist, Lorraine Vaillancourt is the founder and Musical Director of Le Nouvel Ensemble Moderne (NEM), the ensemble-in-residence at the Université de Montréal’s Faculty of Music since 1989. A full professor at this same institution, she also directed the Atelier de musique contemporaine from 1974 until her retirement from teaching in 2016. &nbsp;\r\n\r\nShe is regularly invited as a guest conductor by different ensembles and orchestras both in Canada and abroad. Lorraine Vaillancourt is a founding member, along with composers José Evangelista, John Rea and Claude Vivier, of..."
      }
    ],
