    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Catalão’s first steps in music were with the violin at the age of 7, but it was his passion for hardcore music that led him to the drum set in his teenage years.&nbsp; Then, one summer night, he shaved his long hair, and decided to devote himself to percussion.\r\n\r\nThe cause of this epiphany was Ney Rosauro, with whom he studied at Santa Maria in Brazil before continuing his training, first with Emmanuel Séjourné in Strasbourg, then with Robert Leroux in Montreal.\r\n\r\nWhile refining his skills as a performer, he began to take part in experimental projects.&nbsp; He received awards for..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g13281020",
