    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Known for his “powerful singing” and “considerable mastery of diction”, baritone Clayton Kennedy has had an eclectic career in baroque and early music, has premiered contemporary works of Canadian composers, as well as collaborated with world-renowned artists, studios and producers.\r\n\r\nIn the field of early music and oratorio, he has appeared as a soloist on several occasions with Studio de Musique Ancienne de Montreal (SMAM), as well as Ensemble Caprice, the Choir of the Church of St. Andrew &amp; St. Paul, Bande Montréal Baroque, I Musici de Montréal, Ensemble Vocal Katimavik,..."
