    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Flutist Marilène Provencher-Leduc holds a doctorate in performance from the Université de Montréal (2016) and is also a graduate of the Conservatoire de Musique de Montréal (2010). She currently teaches flute at the Université de Sherbrooke.\r\n\r\nMusically very versatile, she perfected her skills in contemporary music, then integrated klezmer music and improvisation into her instrumental practice. As a result, she was a member of the Eastern European music octet Oktopus between 2010-2020, and performed nationally and internationally (Festival international de Jazz de Montréal 2016 and..."
      }
