    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Huei is a writer, musician, and videographer from New York City. His professional work in the film industry paired with formal training as a classical musician has led him to pursue various forms of media including screenwriting, directing, and composing. In 2016, Huei was an artist-in-residence at the Banff Centre for Arts and Creativity where his collaboration with the Indigenous Leadership Conference produced an acclaimed short film, “Black Earth,” which he shot and directed. From 2017 to 2019, he held a position at Canadian documentary studio Eye Steel Film as a post-production..."
      }
    ],
