    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Stick&Bow"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Stick&amp;Bow, “The trailblazing Montreal duo that plays everything from Bach to Radiohead” (CBC Music’s The Intro), unitesCanadian marimba player Krystina Marcoux and Argentinian cellist Juan Sebastian Delgado. Classically trained musicians,they present a wide spectrum of musical styles, ranging from rock to gypsy-jazz and baroque to tango. Their eclecticrepertoire features original arrangements of some of the most celebrated works in history, highlighting the potential oftheir instruments combined. In their creative process, Stick&amp;Bow combines musical narration with humor..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/PerformingGroup"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g14130660",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/fr/le-vivier/repertoire/estatuas"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/datePublished": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2023"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Estatuas"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/fr/le-vivier/repertoire/estatuas"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\r\nI do not know the names of the statues, but I know that marble has frozen their lives, and that there is something striking from within.\" Esther Ramondelli, De heridas y luciérnagas\r\n\r\n\r\nWhat if we were all like statues locked inside marble, preserving our lives but depriving ourselves of the freedom to express? What if this marble took the name of fear, illness, or simply powerlessness? I tried to imagine what strikes us from the inside, what is alive and seeks a crack to escape. Thus, a fleeting melodic line is born from within. It awakens the most organic sounds, transforming into..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g14130700",
