  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g14635020",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/nirgun-bhajan-ii-villanelles-de-voyelles"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/datePublished": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2022"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": " Nirgun Bhajan II \"Villanelles de Voyelles“"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/nirgun-bhajan-ii-villanelles-de-voyelles"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Dans cette commedia abstraite carnavalesque,les chanteurs imitent des bruits d’oiseaux, génèrent des sons de voix comme des synthétiseurs, se déplacent et interagissent intensément les uns avec les autres -surtout en suivant des instructions qui leur sont relayées à l’oreille. Mais les instructions sont souvent ouvertes et les chanteurs prennent également leurs propres décisions musicales et théâtrales. Ils doivent porter des costumes, au minimum des demi-masques couvrant le haut du visage — puristes ou flamboyants…\r\n"
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g14635060",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/murmuration"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/datePublished": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2024"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Murmuration"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/murmuration"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Murmuration est une ode à l’écoute des sonorités discrètes de notre biodiversité sonore. Le terme fait également référence aux nuées d’oiseaux qui forment des ondulations visuelles dans le ciel, typique des espèces d’oiseaux grégaires comme les étourneaux. Ainsi, c’est une invitation au rassemblement culturelle autour de la découverte et la mise en valeur de nos paysages sonores.\r\n"
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g14635260",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/artists/ensemble-supermusique"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/sameAs": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.facebook.com/productions.supermusique"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/artists/ensemble-supermusique"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Ensemble SuperMusique"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Founded in 1998, the Ensemble SuperMusique (ESM) is directed by Joane Hétu and Danielle Palardy Roger. This variable-geometry ensemble, entirely devoted to the interpretation of contemporary music and improvisation, is one of the rare ensembles whose repertoire consists exclusively of contemporary music. The ESM is made up of the most prominent instrumentalists and composers of Montreal's vibrant contemporary music scene. Since its foundation, the ESM has commissioned more than 50 works that combine written music and improvisation. The Montreal record company DAME has released several of its recordings.\r\n"
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/PerformingGroup"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g14635360",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/artists/la-chorale-joker"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/artists/la-chorale-joker"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "La Chorale Joker"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Founded in 2012 and directed by Joane Hétu, La Chorale Joker is an a cappella choir comprising a dozen vocalists. This unconventional vocal ensemble explores vocal texture and timbre; rhythmic motifs; sound poetry; and extramusical sounds like breath, babbling, and mouth noise. La Chorale Joker is invested in marginal sounds, peripheral territories, and the spaces between the tones of conventional choir singing, and does so not through established repertoire, but by inventing its own language to suit. Joane Hétu guides the singers through improvisation and aleatoric music with a variety..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/PerformingGroup"
    ]
  },
