    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://sixtrum.com/en"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Sixtrum Percussion"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "With roots firmly planted in the major classics that formed the percussion ensemble genre of the 20th Century, today Sixtrum embarks in an unbridled exploration of contemporary percussion. Made up of virtuosic and multi-talented performers, Sixtrum renews its artistic universe through constant confrontation with other art forms and other musical genres. Every collaboration aims to investigate new forms of expression and new modes of presentation that will form new links between music, musicians and audience."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/PerformingGroup"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g14735920",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/celerite"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/datePublished": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2020"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Célérité"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/celerite"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Sound propagates at different speeds depending on its propagation medium. Air and water, two universes with different sound behaviours. It is this metaphor that inspires this piece, where time is compressed, dilated, disintegrated, ellipse.\r\n"
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g14735960",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/jeux-deau"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/datePublished": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2020"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Jeux d’eau"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/jeux-deau"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This work proposes to approach creation and interpretation in a playful way by allowing musicians to interact easily with each other and with real-time sound processing through different open musical \"stages\". The inclusion of toys and non-traditional percussive objects complements these comical intentions with the aim of making contemporary music more accessible for the duration of a concert.\r\n"
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g14736000",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/grand-fracas"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/datePublished": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2020"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "À grand fracas "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/grand-fracas"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Samuel Bobony has a hybrid practice as a drummer and electroacoustic composer. He is interested in the different levels of reality caused by the creation of real-time samplings and the manipulation of their temporality. This makes it possible to freeze out of time the interactive musical gestures between the percussionists of the Sixtrum ensemble and their sound manipulations. Using underwater recordings using hydrophones, the unusual sound loops are then modulated by effects chains designed especially for this work.\r\n&nbsp;\r\n"
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g14736040",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/shui"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/datePublished": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2017"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Shui"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/shui"
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g14736080",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/fishbones"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/datePublished": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2007"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Fishbones"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/fishbones"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\"The sounds that glide through the air carry a certain nostalgia, solitude, anxiety... they sound like human voice! The submerged percussion instruments drown us in an aquatic sonority that crescendo becomes a metallic roar. The cynic idea of fishy life cycle came to me while I was sophisticating this piece, a life that begins with an egg hatching in the ocean freely to end up in a form of pressurized canned food.\" - O. Adamek\r\n"
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
