    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Video Phase"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Video Phase emerges from the collaboration of two innovative musician-creators, Julien-Robert and Julien Compagne. Their shared vision revolves around cultivating a fresh, hybrid artistic genre that seamlessly blends music, video, and technology into a singular entity.\r\n\r\nThey create universes where music and visuals are totally fused, one being the representation of the other and vice-versa. The interactive nature of the visual in their performances enables performers to improvise while preserving the transient essence of a live show. Alongside their stage productions, they also craft..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/PerformingGroup"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g15092120",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/alt-escape"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Alt-Escape"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/alt-escape"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A series of interactive and mesmerizing sonic and visual realms\r\n\r\nAlt-Escape is a one-hour digital performance that immerses the spectator in a series of interactive and mesmerizing sonic and visual realms, delving into concepts of gravity, physics, and time.\r\nThis show harnesses digital technologies to invent interactive instruments from scratch, delivering a distinct aesthetic proposition that seamlessly integrates in real-time music, video projection, and technology, breathing life into a novel concert experience.\r\nIn addition to the stage version, the group is expanding the concept of..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
