    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "5ilience"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "5ilience is a new Montreal-based ensemble of five emerging artists with a passion for chamber music.\r\n\r\nOur quintet, composed of oboe, clarinet, saxophone, bass clarinet and bassoon played respectively by Léanne Teran-Paul, Mariane Pellerin, Thomas Gauthier-Lang, Gwénaëlle Ratouit and Alex Eastley, has established itself as the very first reed quintet in Quebec. It is through the combination the timbral specificities of the instruments in this formation that we have developed a palette of sounds as unique as it is versatile.\r\n\r\nFollowing in the footsteps of the very first reed quintet,..."
      }
    ],
