    ],
    "https://ogp.me/ns#title": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Journées de la Culture - Duo ÉK | Le Vivier"
      }
    ],
    "https://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Let the children shine with Duo ÉK and their show Pouet! — a musical play inviting the audience to participate.Pouet is a sound-filled, humorous play that invites children to dive into the fantastical world of Duo ÉK. While one sleeps soundly, the other begins a most unusual morning routine. Together, they weave a multi-sensory world through three scenes that recount a day unlike any other. In this imaginary universe, young audience members embark on an interactive expedition, punctuated by melodies, sounds, and noises that become messages and excuses to play: mime, word games, and funny sounds to listen to and repeat. With their rich and surprising instruments, the duo ék piques children's curiosity and draws them into an adventure where the energy is contagious. Here, the audience are not mere observers: they become accomplices in a sensory journey at the heart of the action.2:00 p.m.: Performance 13:30 p.m.: Performance 24:30 p.m.: Workshop: Come build your instrument with the ÉK Duo and let's improvise together!Artists :Emilie Fortin: Trumpet, mime, and co-artistic directorKalung Leung: Trombone, mime, and co-artistic director"
      }
    ],
